{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model combining PCA_n2000 RNA encoding with ResNet50 image features via concatenation fusion, achieving 52.66% validation accuracy (vs. 48.5% for the RNA-only baseline). The result suggests multimodal integration may improve performance, though the simple concatenation method lacks complexity to isolate specific benefits. Uncertainty remains about whether image data or the fusion strategy drove improvements, as no comparative analysis with alternative aggregation techniques was conducted."
}

